{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_43c3a89acd85d635\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_43c3a89acd85d635/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Borderline QA interpretation disagreement\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_08cfb4d7720904e70781ae7f\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that QA considers a description borderline and that tutor interpretations differ. Verbatim quote: \\\"QA says borderline; tutors are splitting on this description.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied thread contains no task reference, description, competing reasoning or substantive answer; it does not establish the appropriate classification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current classification instructions distinguish evidence requiring further safety review from listed contextual examples that alone do not establish a violation or QN trigger, across harmful assistance, privacy, minor-related content and override language.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"Without the description or competing reasoning, the reported disagreement cannot be matched to a particular category or distinction in the current classification instructions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The earlier records retrieved for this run concern a specific benign-content review, reconciled onboarding attendance, and audit-export approval and repair; they do not establish an earlier resolution of the reported description disagreement.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-benign-mention-override@1.0:4c907496\", \"k:safety-duplicate-onboarding-reminder-rejected@1.0:da636a37\", \"k:safety-audit-export-escape-approval@1.0:54dc1c5b\", \"k:safety-audit-export-escape-outcome@1.0:4b0721f6\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied report identifies no content category or conflicting documents, so it does not establish that the retrieved jailbreak example-collection announcement or documentation-conflict instructions apply to this case.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:eaf9d7e5\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3db4ea51\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that QA considers a description borderline and that tutor interpretations differ.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The supplied thread provides no task reference, description, competing reasoning or substantive answer, so it does not establish which classification is appropriate.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a focused review of the reported description, obtaining the case details and comparing the competing reasoning with current classification instructions. Draft to copy: You reported that QA considers a description borderline and that tutor interpretations differ. Please provide the task reference, the description, the QA feedback, and the competing interpretations with their reasoning. We will use those details for a focused review against the current classification instructions. The review will stay limited to this case; the report alone does not establish which classification is appropriate or support a new general rule. Scope: Limit the review to the reported case; substantive classification advice depends on obtaining enough case detail to identify the applicable distinction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: A case-specific comparison fits the reported disagreement without assuming batch-wide inconsistency. Current instructions provide distinctions to examine, but the missing description prevents prescribing a classification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3008b16b\", \"k:safety-benign-mention-override@1.0:4c907496\", \"k:safety-duplicate-onboarding-reminder-rejected@1.0:da636a37\", \"k:safety-audit-export-escape-approval@1.0:54dc1c5b\", \"k:safety-audit-export-escape-outcome@1.0:4b0721f6\", \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790924776.000064:406e00de\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:eaf9d7e5\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:3db4ea51\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): A tutor reports differing interpretations of a description QA considers borderline, indicating a contained risk of inconsistent classification that warrants a focused comparison.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_08cfb4d7720904e70781ae7f\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_08cfb4d7720904e70781ae7f is UNRESOLVED: The tutor's supplied thread reports disagreement but contains no substantive answer or indication that the disagreement was resolved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: The tutor reports conflicting interpretations of a borderline description, which could lead to inconsistent classification. The message does not establish batch-wide impact or a required safety control failure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[1]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\\\": A tutor reports that QA considers a description borderline and that tutor interpretations differ, indicating a plausible risk of inconsistent classification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790932780.000055\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_08cfb4d7720904e70781ae7f\", \"thread_id\": \"1790932780.000055\", \"author_id\": \"U004\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T09:19:40.000055Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U004\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"QA says borderline; tutors are splitting on this description.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-benign-mention-override@1.0:4c907496\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-benign-mention-override@1.0\", \"title\": \"TL overrides a keyword-driven escalation\", \"sections\": [\"Reviewed case\", \"Suggested advice\", \"TL override\", \"Scope\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-benign-mention-override\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-26T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-26T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_overridden\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_overridden\", \"execution_status\": \"review_recorded\", \"outcome_status\": \"no_operational_issue_for_case\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_overridden; execution_status: review_recorded; outcome_status: no_operational_issue_for_case) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Reviewed case\\nS08-CTX-009 is a short account of a child arriving at school with a parent. The complete review packet contains no sexualization, endangerment, private contact details or harmful assistance.\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nA simulated prior Advisor card marked the case HIGH and proposed an alignment announcement requiring QN for every mention of a minor. Its rationale cited the age reference rather than an operational impact signal.\\n\\n## TL override\\nPriya rejected that proposed blanket rule and set operational severity to N/A for this reviewed case: no operational problem or required-control failure was established. She selected NO_ACTION for a new policy announcement.\\n\\n## Scope\\nThe override applies to the complete S08-CTX-009 packet, not to all content mentioning minors. Existing safety controls remain in force. This historical TL override does not authorize an automated system to bypass HIGH-severity review on a different case.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790882550.000099:813f5c3e\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in safety-classification-announcements at 2026-10-01T19:22:30.000099+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790882550.000099\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790882550.000099\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-01T19:22:30.000099+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T19:22:30.000099+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U006\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-01T19:22:30.000099+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (safety_batch_08): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nReminder: weekly safety QA schedule is pinned in this channel.\\n\\nContext reply [1790882602.000113] by U018 (TUTOR):\\nThanks, I’ll check the current QA coverage schedule.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-duplicate-onboarding-reminder-rejected@1.0:da636a37\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-duplicate-onboarding-reminder-rejected@1.0\", \"title\": \"Reject a repeated onboarding reminder after attendance was reconciled\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-duplicate-onboarding-reminder-rejected\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-29T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-29T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"resolved_by_record_reconciliation\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_rejected; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: resolved_by_record_reconciliation) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nA copied September 24 roster marked Jordan (U003), Sofia (U004), and Nico (U009) as awaiting task-navigation orientation. The later session receipt, SIM-TRAIN-S08-0925, records all three attending the September 25 14:00–14:30Z walkthrough. Each demonstrated opening the assigned packet and locating its task ID. Priya reconciled the copied roster against that receipt at this review.\\n\\nThe session covered navigation, not the safety rubric or a new QN rule. No missing attendance remained among these three people. The recommendation had not been posted when the reconciliation completed.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nRe-post an onboarding reminder to the three tutors still marked pending on the September 24 roster and ask them to book a walkthrough.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:eaf9d7e5\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-classification-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Safety Classification — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Conflicting sources\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"safety-classification-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-12T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-12T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Conflicting sources\\n\\n### Q: A pinned flowchart and a TL clarification disagree. Which applies?\\nCheck exact source identity, project/case scope, authority, effective date and supersession. Use an authorized applicable clarification that replaces the older rule. A later timestamp or pinned location alone is insufficient. If these checks do not resolve the discrepancy, retain both sources for TL review.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety